<title>USA: US OATS HARVEST SEEN AS THIRD-LOWEST IN HISTORY.</title>
<headline>US OATS HARVEST SEEN AS THIRD-LOWEST IN HISTORY.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. oat production for 1997 is expected to be the third lowest harvest since U.S. Agriculture Department first began keeping records in 1866, the department said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Production for this year was forecast at 187 million bushels in the USDA's monthly crop report, up two pct from the USDA's previous forecast in July. The forecasted harvest would also be up 21 percent from last year, the department said.</p>
<p>The forecasted yield for U.S. fields was 58.1 bushels per acre, up 1.4 bushels from July because of timely rainfall that improved the crop condition, the department said.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
